{"status":"unsupported_domain","reason":"A faithful executable contract for the frozen obligations cannot be expressed in the specified typed AST and admitted Python generated-test bridge.","gaps":[{"obligations":["D1","A1"],"description":"The input edges are JSON arrays [u,v,cost] with positional meaning. The frontend provides homogeneous lists and named records, but no fixed heterogeneous tuple or registered conversion preserving these arrays and their exact representation."},{"obligations":["O1","O2","O3","O4","O5","S1"],"description":"Each output entry is an integer, JSON null, or the exact string \"-inf\". The specified sort grammar lacks this scalar union and JSON null. Unit, String, records, and Except do not supply the required JSON representation; replacing entries with tagged records, strings, or result values would change observable behavior."},{"obligations":["S2","R1"],"description":"The formula grammar cannot state Python file placement, dependency restrictions, absence of external I/O, or absence of retained cross-call state. Pure mathematical function semantics alone do not establish these implementation requirements."}],"preserved_obligations":["D1","A1","O1","O2","O3","O4","O5","S1","S2","R1"],"required_extension":"Provide registered executable representations for positional edge triples and distance entries serialized exactly as integer, null, or \"-inf\", together with implementation checks for solution.py, purity, external I/O, retained state, and standard-library-only dependencies. All frozen graph semantics, examples, and assumption satisfiability requirements remain required.","lean_source":null,"formalization":null}